# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=skyward spec=priest:discipline style=wander
# size=10 difficulty=normal view=1280x800 save=fresh
#
# boss=skyward is a coverage label only -- `evening` steers at no boss, so
# this walks in at the door same as every other mode=walk entry on [[#6]].
# Checked sessions.jsonl and direction.md's hypothesis 6 first: wander+
# 10-normal+fresh+1280x800 is the exact recurring cell that opened #6/#281
# (druid:guardian, 2026-09-25-17.play: parked in THE VIGIL at hero=
# (274.5,-1572.7), no wipe, bill hits=0 taken=0) and has been re-run twice
# since on different classes -- mage:frost (2026-09-26-23.play) and
# warlock:destruction (2026-10-01-3.play) -- both of which instead wiped to
# the corridor's watchmen and then hit #271's retry-never-restarts wall.
# Zero clean 10-normal wander crossings are on record for this cell. All
# three priors were a tank or a dps; this is the first healer run through
# it, and priest:discipline's own kit (self-mitigation, a direct self-heal)
# is the one that most plausibly survives the watchmen long enough to find
# out whether the stall-without-wiping shape or the wipe-and-stuck shape is
# what a body that does not die here meets.
open
targets
shot front
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:priest:discipline
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot arrive-threshold

evening wander 300 10
state
shot after-evening
bill
